## Tool Name: run_smbclient
### Description: Run smbclient to connect to an SMB/CIFS server and optionally execute commands.
Operations include things like getting files from the server to the local machine, putting files from the local machine to the server, retrieving directory information from the server and so on.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'target': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The target IP address or NetBIOS name.'}, 'service': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The name of the SMB service to connect to (e.g. the name of a share or a printer).'}, 'username': {'default': 'guest', 'type': 'string', 'description': 'The username for authentication. If not provided, defaults to "guest".'}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'The password required to access the specified service on the specified server. If not provided, no password will be used (\'-N\' for anonymous access). If empty string "", forces an empty password via \'user%\'. If a string is provided, uses that password.'}, 'command': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': 'ls', 'description': 'Semicolon-separated list of commands to be executed.'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Additional arguments for smbclient (e.g. '-p 139')."}, 'timeout': {'default': 120, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum time in seconds that the command is allowed to run for (default is 120 seconds).'}}, 'required': ['target', 'service'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_getnpusers
### Description: Run Impacket's GetNPUsers.py to list and get TGTs for users vulnerable to AS-REP roasting (that have pre-authentication disabled).
For those users with such configuration, an output file will be generated so you can send it for cracking.
If 'usersfile' is omitted, the script will automatically attempt to identify user accounts with pre-authentication disabled via LDAP using the provided credentials. If no 'usersfile' and credentials are provided, it will attempt to retrieve users through an RPC null session.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'domain': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Target domain (e.g., 'corp.local')."}, 'username': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Username for authenticated bind (optional).'}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Password for authentication (optional).'}, 'usersfile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Path to file containing a list of usernames to test (optional). One username per line must be specified (just the username, no domain needed).'}, 'dc_ip': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Domain controller IP address (recommended). If omitted, the positional argument's domain part will be used (in that case, it must be a Fully-Qualified-Domain-Name (FQDN))."}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Additional arguments for GetNPUsers.py.'}, 'timeout': {'default': 120, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Max execution time in seconds.'}}, 'required': ['domain'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_getuserspns
### Description: Run Impacket's GetUserSPNs.py to enumerate service accounts that have an SPN and obtain their password hash to perform Kerberoasting.
The obtained password hashes will be saved to a provided output file.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'domain': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Target domain (e.g., 'corp.local')."}, 'username': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Username for authentication.'}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Password for authentication.'}, 'dc_ip': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Domain controller IP address. If omitted, the positional argument's domain part will be used (in that case, it must be a Fully-Qualified-Domain-Name (FQDN))."}, 'no_preauth': {'default': False, 'type': 'boolean', 'description': "Option to indicate that the user with 'username' is vulnerable to AS-REP roasting and the Kerberoast attack should be performed without pre-authentication."}, 'use_kerberos': {'default': False, 'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Use Kerberos authentication (-k). This option requires either a password or a hash to be provided.'}, 'hash_': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'LM and/or NT hash to use for authentication. The format is as follows: [LMhash]:NThash (the LM hash is optional, the NT hash must be prepended with a colon (:)'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Additional arguments for GetUserSPNs.py.'}, 'timeout': {'default': 120, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Max execution time in seconds.'}}, 'required': ['domain', 'username'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_kerbrute
### Description: Run kerbrute for Kerberos-based user enumeration and password spraying.
Modes:
    - 'userenum'     : Enumerate valid usernames. This does not cause any login failures so it will not lock out any accounts.
    - 'passwordspray': Spray a single password against many users. This will increment the failed login count and lock out accounts if used excessively.
    - 'bruteforce'   : Bruteforce passwords for users. This will increment the failed login count and lock out accounts if used excessively.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'domain': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Target domain (e.g., 'corp.local')."}, 'dc_ip': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Domain controller IP address. If blank, will lookup via DNS.'}, 'mode': {'enum': ['userenum', 'passwordspray', 'bruteforce'], 'type': 'string', 'description': "Kerbrute mode ('userenum', 'passwordspray', 'bruteforce')."}, 'usersfile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Path to file containing usernames.'}, 'bruteforcefile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Path to file containing username and password combinations (for bruteforce) in the format 'username:password'."}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Single password (for passwordspray).'}, 'safe': {'default': False, 'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Enable safe mode (avoid account lockouts). When this option is enabled, if an account comes back as locked out, it will abort all threads to stop locking out any other accounts. Default: False.'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Additional kerbrute arguments.'}, 'timeout': {'default': 300, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Max execution time in seconds. Default: 300 seconds.'}}, 'required': ['domain', 'dc_ip', 'mode'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_hashcat
### Description: Run hashcat for password cracking.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'hash_file': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'File containing hashes.'}, 'hash_mode': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Hash type (-m), e.g. 18200 (AS-REP), 13100 (Kerberoast).'}, 'outputfile': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Output file for cracked hashes.'}, 'attack_mode': {'default': 0, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Attack mode (-a), e.g. 0 (straight), 3 (mask).'}, 'wordlist': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Path to wordlist file (for -a 0).'}, 'mask': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Mask string (for -a 3), e.g. '?l?l?l?l?d?d'."}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Additional hashcat arguments.'}, 'timeout': {'default': 600, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Max execution time in seconds.'}}, 'required': ['hash_file', 'hash_mode', 'outputfile'], 'type': 'object'}```

